{"id":"959aea8b-469f-49ea-95e5-e5ee1f7a8f00","object":"chat.completion","created":1784840684,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    accepted = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        parseable = call['parseable']\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / max(tokens, 1)\\n        is_accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        if is_accepted:\\n            accepted.append(call_id)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'gain': round(gain, 6),\\n            'normalized_gain': round(normalized_gain, 6),\\n            'parseable': parseable,\\n            'accepted': is_accepted\\n        })\\n    return {\\n        'accepted': accepted,\\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" mapping to a Python source string. The source defines a function `solve(case)` that processes the given case payload. The task: filter API calls based on normalized gain (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) normalized by at least one prediction token (i.e., divide by max(prediction_tokens, 1) presumably, but the spec says \"normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" meaning divide by prediction_tokens, but ensure denominator is at least 1? Actually \"by at least one prediction token\" could mean divide by the number of prediction tokens, and if zero? But prediction_tokens is given, likely positive. But to be safe, use max(1, prediction_tokens). Also require parseable true. Normalized gain >= threshold. Then return accepted call IDs (list of st